Version 0.2.1
~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Released: 2026-11-02

Features:
 * Malachi Mail checks once a day whether a newer version is available
   and shows a bar with what is new, a download link, Remind Me Later
   and Skip This Version; a security release asks once. The check sends
   the program's version and package to its website, nothing else, and
   can be turned off in Preferences → General → Updates, where Check Now
   asks at once.

Version 0.2.0
~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Released: 2026-11-01

Notes:
 * The macOS disk image is now signed with a Developer ID and notarised
   by Apple, so it opens like any downloaded app. The first start after
   an earlier build asks once for each stored password: choose Always
   Allow.
 * The Windows installers are still unsigned, so SmartScreen warns once.
   There is no portable zip for Windows any more.
 * Every file of a release is named alike, with the version, the system
   and the architecture: Malachi-Mail-0.2.0-windows-x64-setup.exe.

Features:
 * Address books: the contacts of Microsoft 365 and of CardDAV servers in
   a Contacts window, where they can be searched, edited and added, with
   their photos. A CalDAV server may now offer only address books.
 * An address in a message can be shown as a contact or added to the
   contacts, and contacts are suggested while you write.
 * Contact photos are shown beside the sender in the message list,
   conversations, the chat and the Board.
 * Moving mail to the Trash, the archive, Junk or another folder, also
   from the Board, can be undone with Ctrl+Z (⌘Z on a Mac) or from the
   message that confirms it.
 * AI agents can search and read contacts through the MCP bridge, and
   create or change them only with your explicit permission.

Bugfixes:
 * A chat opens at its newest message.
 * The conversation of a case on the Board shows its cards as soon as
   they are loaded.
 * The Board takes new correspondents into account after new mail.
 * eWay-CRM accepts a web service address over http on this computer.
 * The assistant in the app reaches your mail from its first answer.
 * On macOS, the preview of a rewrite shows its answer from the start.
 * On Windows, cards and status colours follow the window's theme.

Version 0.1.2
~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Released: 2026-10-26

Bugfixes:
 * The macOS app builds again with Xcode 26.6.
 * Fixed tests of meeting invitations that depended on the date they ran
   on.

Version 0.1.1
~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Released: 2026-10-26

Notes:
 * Malachi Mail now also runs on Windows 11 and macOS, with a native
   window on each. It is still an early version: keep a second mail
   program for anything that matters.

Features:
 * Gmail and Google Workspace accounts, through GNOME Online Accounts or
   a sign-in in the browser; Microsoft 365 can sign in in the browser too.
 * Conversations: the message list can be grouped by conversation, and a
   conversation is shown as cards on a timeline or as a chat, with your
   own replies from Sent and unsent drafts in place.
 * A quick reply under a message or a chat, without opening a window.
 * Search of the stored mail, as you type, in a folder, an account or
   all accounts.
 * Several messages can be selected and archived, moved, deleted, marked
   or forwarded together; messages and folders have context menus.
 * Recipients are shown as removable badges while you write.
 * Plain text that looks like Markdown is pasted as formatted text.
 * Newsletters and mailing lists are recognised and can be unsubscribed
   from with one click where the sender allows it.
 * Jira issues can be followed as conversations: comments, status changes
   and replies from Malachi Mail, and Jira notification mail can be hidden.
 * A calendar for Microsoft 365 and CalDAV servers, with invitations
   answered from the message and reminders.
 * The Board sorts conversations that wait for you, wait for others or are
   just for your information, with reminders, Done and archive.
 * eWay-CRM: messages can be saved to the CRM with links to contacts,
   companies, deals and projects, and saved conversations followed.
 * An assistant (Claude Code or ChatGPT, run on your own account) can
   summarise mail, rewrite what you write, turn your words into a search,
   suggest replies and sort the Board; a profile tells it about you.
 * An MCP bridge lets AI agents read your mail and write drafts; changing
   or sending mail needs your explicit permission.
 * Mail can be stored compressed, and attachments of older mail left on
   the server or never stored at all.
 * A server certificate can be trusted explicitly by its fingerprint.

Version 0.1.0
~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Released: 2026-09-06

Notes:
 * First tagged release. Mail can be read, written and sent, but this is
   still an early version: keep a second mail program for anything that
   matters.

Features:
 * IMAP accounts with a setup assistant that finds the server settings for
   most providers; passwords are kept in the system keyring.
 * Mail is synchronised for offline reading, with new messages arriving as
   the server announces them.
 * Writing and sending, with formatted text, attachments and inline
   images. A message that cannot be sent right away waits in the outbox
   and is retried; a copy is filed in Sent.
 * Microsoft 365 and Outlook.com accounts through GNOME Online Accounts,
   with no separate sign-in.
 * HTML mail is cleaned before it is shown, and remote images stay blocked
   until you ask for them or trust the sender. Attached messages open in a
   window of their own.
 * Attachments can be opened, saved one by one or saved all at once.
 * The message list can be narrowed to unread or flagged messages.
 * The folder sidebar can be folded, and folders pinned to Favourites.
 * Recipients are completed from the system address books and from the
   people you have written to before.
 * Czech translation.

Notes:
 * Search and conversation threading are not available yet.
 * Gmail accounts are not supported yet.
